{
  "id": "sglang-qwen3.6-35b-a3b-exl3-offload-mtp-256k-rtx-a2000-laptop-8gb",
  "engine": "sglang",
  "about": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (yeasah EXL3) on an RTX A2000 8GB Laptop GPU (35 W) with trellis-serve MoE offload: the routed experts stay in pinned host RAM and stream into a GPU expert cache, everything else runs on the card. Changes from the rtx-3060-ti-8gb launch: the full 262,144-token context, the checkpoint's MTP layer as a one-token NEXTN draft (an EXL3 target needs the image's hot-token map for the draft head), --mem-fraction-static 0.80 (0.85 runs out of memory with the draft) and --chunked-prefill-size 2048 (4096 runs out of memory in prefill with the draft). Measured on a ThinkPad P1 Gen 5 (i7-12700H, 32 GB single-channel DDR5), 30 s decode runs: 24.7 tok/s and 1,409 tok/s prefill without the draft, 26.8 tok/s and 1,206 tok/s prefill with it; KV pool about 230K tokens.",
